{
  "_comment": [
    "Multi-channel config. Copy to channels.json and fill in each channel's creds.",
    "One niche per channel, each with its OWN Google Cloud project, OAuth client and token,",
    "because YouTube's Data API quota is ~6 uploads/day per Cloud project.",
    "",
    "For each channel: create the YouTube channel, make a Cloud project, enable the",
    "YouTube Data API v3 and YouTube Analytics API, make an OAuth client, download its",
    "client_secret.json to the client_secrets path below, then run:",
    "   venv/bin/python scripts/youtube_oauth.py --channel <slug> --force",
    "which writes that channel's token. Doctor (scripts/growth.py doctor) reports each channel.",
    "",
    "Set CHANNELS_FILE=channels.json in .env. A channel with enabled=false is skipped;",
    "set it true once its token is in place. Feeds are the source creators clipped for that niche."
  ],
  "channels": [
    {
      "slug": "tech",
      "name": "Tech & Science",
      "niche": "tech reviews, gadgets, science and engineering",
      "brand_name": "@your-tech-handle",
      "client_secrets": "secrets/tech_client_secret.json",
      "token_path": "secrets/tech_token.json",
      "uploads_per_day": 3,
      "timezone": "Asia/Kolkata",
      "require_approval": true,
      "enabled": false,
      "feeds": [
        "https://www.youtube.com/@mkbhd",
        "https://www.youtube.com/@Mrwhosetheboss",
        "https://www.youtube.com/@MarkRober"
      ]
    },
